0 @N92@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Aaron Lufkin Dennison - American Watchmaker, a pioneer in industrial watch manufacturing, an inventor, and founder of several companies.  Aaron's father was Andrew Dennison, a boot and shoemaker, who was also a music teacher. From an early age, Aar
1 CONC on was interested in mass production, and from the age of 18 to about 27 he apprenticed in various jewelry and watch repair, and manufacturing divisions. One of the first companies he created, Dennison Manufacturing Company, made paper boxes for je
1 CONC welry under the supervision of his younger brother, Eliphalet Dennison.  It operated under that name until 1990 when it merged with Avery International Corporation and became Avery Dennison. One of his businesses was was located in Birmingham, Engl
1 CONC and.  It was very successful and continued in operation until 1967, under various names including Dennison, Wigley & Company, named to include his partner Alfred Wigley, who joined him in 1879. Franklin Dennison, Aaron's son, became a partner in th
1 CONC e firm after his father died. The company was renamed, The Dennison Watch Case Company, 10 years after Aaron's death. It was in operation until 1967.   Find A Grave Memorial# 132070892
