0 @N167@ NOTE The tomb of
1 CONT Peter Johnson
1 CONT Who fell asleep
1 CONT Sep. 4th 1844.
1 CONT In the 94th year of his age:
1 CONT he was an affectionate Husband
1 CONT A kind Father, 
1 CONT A sympathizing Friend,
1 CONT A noble Patriot, a brave Soldier,
1 CONT And a devoted Christian;
1 CONT Like Abraham it may in truth be said of him,
1 CONT “he died in a good old age, an
1 CONT Old man and full of years
1 CONT And was gathered to his Fathers”
1 CONT Having served his country 
1 CONT during her revolutionary struggle
1 CONT in liberty under Washington, 
1 CONT having professed his Faith in 
1 CONT Jesus Christ while under the
1 CONT Pastoral care of William Tennent
1 CONT And having acted as a ruling
1 CONT Elder in the First Presbyterian
1 CONT Church of Freehold for more
1 CONT Than half a century,
1 CONT He fell asleep in Jesus
1 CONT In the full hope of a part in
1 CONT the first resurrection
