0 @N519@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT REF: http://www.haskellfamilyhistory.com/haskell/4/96093.html
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas HASKELL
1 CONT 
1 CONT Born: 27 Jan 1714/15, Rochester,Plymouth,Massachusetts,United States
1 CONT Marriage (1): Hannah GOSS on 12 Nov 1742 in Brookfield,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States
1 CONT Marriage (2): Joanna HUNT on 1 Mar 1748/49 in Greenwich,Hampshire,Massachusetts,United States
1 CONT Died: 30 Dec 1804, Wilmington,Windham,Vermont,United States at age 89
1 CONT 
1 CONT Spouses/Children: 
1 CONT 1. Hannah GOSS 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Hannah HASKELL+
1 CONT Alice HASKELL
1 CONT Lois HASKELL+
1 CONT 
1 CONT 2. Joanna HUNT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Joanna HASKELL+
1 CONT Rhoda HASKELL
1 CONT Thomas HASKELL, Sr.+
1 CONT Andrew HASKELL+
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas married Hannah GOSS, daughter of Philip GOSS and Keziah COOLEY, on 12 Nov 1742 in Brookfield,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States. (Hannah GOSS was born on 4 Sep 1726 in Brookfield,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States,1 2 8 died on 15 Ma
1 CONC y 1749 in Hardwick,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States 1 2 3 8 and was buried in Hardwick,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas next married Joanna HUNT on 1 Mar 1748/49 in Greenwich,Hampshire,Massachusetts,United States.1 2 3 (Joanna HUNT was born on 27 Jul 1716 in Brookfield,Worcester,Massachusetts,United States,1 died on 19 Oct 1793 in Wilmington,Windham,Vermont,U
1 CONC nited States and was buried in Wilmington,Windham,Vermont,United States.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  General Notes:
1 CONT 
1 CONT THE WILMINGTON, VERMONT FAMILY
1 CONT Thomas (4) and his brother Zachariah went to Hardwick along with the others and married sisters. Thomas married first, Hannah Goss, the daughter of Phillip, who died in 1749 at the age of twenty-five. He married second, Joanna Hunt. His daughter Jo
1 CONC anna married Roger Haskell ... The child born on December 20, 1753 is given in the table the way I read the record as Rhoda, but it was possibly a son Roger, or there may have been two children, twins. A Roger is listed in the Wilmington Gazetteer
1 CONC , 1884 as having been raised there and Thomas is given therein as having sons Roger, Thomas, and Andrew. Thomas moved to Wilmington in 1779 and had a farm on road 67. His son, Thomas Jr., married Priscilla and had a daughter Rachel ( Note- IGI reco
1 CONC rd: born 1784). However, there is another complication. The gravestone of Thomas' wife Joanna, gives her death as October 19, 1793 so who is the Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Sr. who had a son Alden, born on July 27, 1784, and Lewis, April 19, 1787? I
1 CONC t would appear to be another family yet they seem to be part of the group who bought land in Livingston County, New York in 1847 along with the Haskells whom we know to be Andrew's family. A possibility might be Thomas, son of "Savory House Mark,
1 CONC " who moved away from Rochester, for we do not know when or where he or his wife Deborah died.
1 CONT From Chronicles of the HASKELL Family, by Ira J. Haskell, Ellis Printing Co., Lynn, MA 1943
1 CONT pages 138-139: 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Andrew (5) married Chloe Freeman and followed his father to Vermont in 1780. He was one of the grantees of the town of Sommerset.
1 CONT Lucius or Lucian (6) was the father of Andrew Lucius (7) who died in Amity Township, Pennsylvania His descendants lived in northeastern Pennsylvania and New York State. Captain Thomas (6) moved to Strawberry Point, Iowa and possibly a brother wen
1 CONC t with him. Hori (6) married Laura Bellows, a widow of L. Stevens, and had four childern. She married twice after h is death. Andrew (6) had five children and we note the daughter Elmira who married James Keye of Runney, New Hampshire because it i
1 CONC s easy to mix her with her Aunt Almira. Hiram (6) is shown in the 1884 record as "living on road 36 and having had eleven children with numberless descendants hereabouts." He headed the firm of Haskell and Sons, the latter being Hiram 2nd and Henr
1 CONC y.
1 CONT Ancestor chart of Richard M. Snethen compiled by Richard M. Snethen for the Haskell Family Association.
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Thomas Haskell, born Jan 27, 1715 or 16, is said to have removed from Hardwick to this town about 1779. He had several children, all of whom were born previous to 1758.Andrew Haskell, the youngest child, was baptized in Hardwick April 10, 1757, an
1 CONC d came to Wilmington with his father. Thomas is said to have settled on the farm now owned by David Ballou. Andrew was the father of Hiram, who formerly lived on the farm just across Red Bridge on the Dover road; and also of Andrew,Jr., who lived o
1 CONC n the farm now occupied by Danidl-sic- Medbury."
1 CONT from the book "Reunion of the sons and daughters of the town of Wilmington" http://search.ancestry.com.au
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Thomas HASKELL came from Hardwick, Mass., at an early day, and was the first settler on the farm on road 67, where David BALLOU now lives. He raised three sons, Thomas, Roger and Andrew, the latter of whom served during the Revolution under Washin
1 CONC gton. Hiram HASKELL, son of Andrew, who had eleven children, was born in 1800, and now lives on road 36, in this town. He is the oldest surviving member of the family, which has numerous descendants."...
1 CONT "The Union Congregational Church, located at Wilmington village, was organised by Thomas Haskell, Edward Foster,Perry Swift, and Nathan Foster, in 1780, Rev. Winslow Packard being the first settled pastor."
1 CONT Gazetteer section 304
1 CONT http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~vermont/WindhamWilmington.html 
1 CONT 
