1 CONC ow known as Magnolia Farm. This eventually grew to about 400 acres.  He appears to have been very active in both church and worldy affairs and to have accumulated various properties in this and adjoining counties, including dock and store propertie
1 CONC s at Matawan. In his will he mentions his wife, Agnes. She was probably a second wife and not the mother of his children. He died in 1729, leaving sons; Peter (5), a merchant of Freehold, who died intestate in 1712; William (6); Richard (7), Gavi
1 CONC n (8), and David (9). There may have been daughters
