0 @N1086@ NOTE === !PRF CD #7_James FOSTER !Stephen HOPKINS ===
1 CONT !PRF CD #7_James FOSTER !Stephen HOPKINS-Mayflower Famlies Thru Five Gene.-pg. 105 & 106-Ruth MERRICK b. Eastham in 1684; d. Harwich 13 Feb 1766 in 83rd yr., bur. Old Cem., Brewster.  She m/1 Harwich 2 Nov 1710 Samuel SEARS b. Harwich 15 Sep 1687
1 CONC ; d. there bet. 26 Nov 1726 and 20 Jan 1726/7; s/o Samuel SEARS/Mercy MAYO.  She m/2 Harwich 7 Dec 1731 Chillingsworth FOSTER b. Marshfield 11 Jul 1680; d. Harwich 22 Dec 1764 in 85th yr., bur Old Cem., Brewster; s/o John FOSTER/Mary CHILLINGSWORTH
1 CONC .  He m/1 Marcy FREEMAN b. Eastham 3 Aug 1687, d. Harwich 7 Jul 1720 in 33rd yr., d/o John FREEMAN/Sarah MERRICK and a desc of Pilgrrim William BREWSTER.  He m/2 Susahhan (GRAY) SEARS b. prob. Harwich ca. 1694; d. Harwich 7 Dec 1730, ae 36 yrs.; d/
1 CONC o John GRAY/Susanna CLARKE  Susanna m/1 Harwich 10 Oct 1712 Nathaniel SEARS.  By his first wife Chillingsworth had the following FOSTER ch:  rec Harwich:  James ( b. 21 Jan 1705/06), Chillingsworth (b. 25 Dec 1707), Mary (b. 5 Jan 1709/10), Thoma
1 CONC s (b. 17 Jun 1711/12), Nathan (b. 10 Jun 1715), Isaac (b. 17 Jun 1718), and Marcy (b. 29 Jul 1722), Nathaniel (b. 17 Apr 1725), Jerushah (b. 9 Dec 1727), and a stillborn son (Mar 1729/30).  Dau. Ruth SEARS is mentioned in her father's will of 1723
1 CONC .  Samuel SEARS, Jr. and his wife were admitted to Brewster Church 18 Sep 1715, and the three oldest children were bp. there 16 Oct 1715.  Samuel SEARS Jr. res. in "First Remove" of Harwich in 1726.  Chillingsworth FORSTER, blacksmith and Ruth hi
1 CONC s wife, seamstress, on 3 Feb 1741/2 conveyed land in Eastham that had been owned by "our Honoured Father Mr. William MIRRICK, late of Hariwh."  Chillinsworth FOSTER was a deacon of Brewster Church and held many town offices at Harwich.  The will o
1 CONC f Samuel SEARS Jr., dated 26 Nov 1726 and proved 20 Jan 1726/27, called testator" sick and weak" mentioned wife Ruth (esecutrix), sons Samuel 3rd and Seth Jr. (under 18), and brother Judah SEARS (executor).  An inventory, dated 13 Feb 1726/7, was s
1 CONC worn to by executors 15  Aug 1727.  ...  The will of his father Samuel SEARS, yeoman of Harwich, dated 7 Apr 1740 and proved 6 Mar 1741/2 mentioned, anong others, grandsons Samuel and Seth SEARS(sons of son Samuel deceased), and granddaus. Abigai
1 CONC l HALE, Mercy HOWES, Ruth SEARS, Desire FREEMAN, Mary SNOW and Hannah FOSTER.  ...  The will of Chillingsworth FOSTER of Harwich dated 30 Set 1763 and proved 12 Mar 1765, mentioned wife Ruth; sons Nathan, Isaac, Nathaniel, Chillingsworth (executor
1 CONC ) and Thomas; and daus. Jerusha FOSTER, Mary PADDOCK and Mercy CROSBIE.
